@[lilo page]
LILO, the classic LInux LOader, boots BIOS machines only (not UEFI), from an
MBR (dos) disk. It isn't on this ISO: cast it with network (see
@[todo boot-loader]). LILO records where the kernel lies on the disk, so run
@[lilo] again after every change to the kernel or to /etc/lilo.conf.

In @[enchantment chroot], write /etc/lilo.conf (your disk, root partition and
kernel version; /etc/lilo.example.conf has more options):
  boot=/dev/sda
  prompt
  timeout=50
  default=smgl
  image=/boot/vmlinuz-6.18.59
      label=smgl
      root=/dev/sda2
      read-only
Then install it to the disk's boot sector:
 @[lilo -v]
 @[exit]

Not yet tested on this ISO: please report what works and what doesn't.

Type @[next] to go on to the user setup (or @[todo] for the boot-loader step).
